  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 5.649,
   "e": 8.111,
   "text": "The Modular Emergence Paradox.",
   "dur": 2.462,
   "voiced": 147,
   "sim": 0.805,
   "f0": 136.483,
   "st": 1.111,
   "range_st": 9.495,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 9.096,
   "e": 19.144,
   "text": "If self-organization, local plasticity, and continuous topological rewiring are the proven mechanisms of biological cognition,",
   "dur": 10.048,
   "voiced": 597,
   "sim": 0.883,
   "f0": 126.936,
   "st": -0.145,
   "range_st": 8.855,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 19.441,
   "e": 27.793,
   "text": "why did decades of research into dynamic neural graphs fail to produce modern foundational models?",
   "dur": 8.352,
   "voiced": 516,
   "sim": 0.875,
   "f0": 123.094,
   "st": -0.677,
   "range_st": 6.357,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 28.805,
   "e": 29.898,
   "text": "And conversely,",
   "dur": 1.092,
   "voiced": 66,
   "sim": 0.641,
   "f0": 158.87,
   "st": 3.74,
   "range_st": 11.064,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 30.387,
   "e": 42.987,
   "text": "why did the Transformer, an architecture that violently rejects biological realism with its brute-force all-to-all attention matrices and uniform backpropagation,",
   "dur": 12.6,
   "voiced": 694,
   "sim": 0.861,
   "f0": 126.057,
   "st": -0.265,
   "range_st": 7.464,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 43.538,
   "e": 47.654,
   "text": "conquer every single domain of modern intelligence?",
   "dur": 4.115,
   "voiced": 282,
   "sim": 0.863,
   "f0": 125.053,
   "st": -0.403,
   "range_st": 6.044,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 48.655,
   "e": 52.094,
   "text": "Examine the stark contradiction before us.",
   "dur": 3.439,
   "voiced": 189,
   "sim": 0.779,
   "f0": 117.715,
   "st": -1.45,
   "range_st": 5.222,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 53.028,
   "e": 59.277,
   "text": "Self-organizing networks promised organic modularity and continuous adaptation.",
   "dur": 6.249,
   "voiced": 374,
   "sim": 0.829,
   "f0": 125.388,
   "st": -0.357,
   "range_st": 6.715,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 59.856,
   "e": 71.268,
   "text": "Yet in practice, as these networks scale, they inevitably collapse into representational chaos, destructive interference, or catastrophic forgetting.",
   "dur": 11.412,
   "voiced": 560,
   "sim": 0.815,
   "f0": 135.121,
   "st": 0.937,
   "range_st": 7.949,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 72.035,
   "e": 80.313,
   "text": "Meanwhile, the Transformer, constructed from static, dense, homogeneous matrix multiplications,",
   "dur": 8.277,
   "voiced": 380,
   "sim": 0.817,
   "f0": 133.19,
   "st": 0.688,
   "range_st": 7.516,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 80.613,
   "e": 84.82,
   "text": "spontaneously discovers internal modularity.",
   "dur": 4.207,
   "voiced": 249,
   "sim": 0.84,
   "f0": 134.119,
   "st": 0.808,
   "range_st": 6.794,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 85.599,
   "e": 91.977,
   "text": "Inside a trained Transformer, researchers in mechanistic interpretability have uncovered",
   "dur": 6.377,
   "voiced": 374,
   "sim": 0.808,
   "f0": 135.277,
   "st": 0.957,
   "range_st": 8.143,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 92.317,
   "e": 101.808,
   "text": "sophisticated induction heads, modular routing circuits, arithmetic units, and in-context associative recall mechanisms.",
   "dur": 9.491,
   "voiced": 487,
   "sim": 0.86,
   "f0": 132.563,
   "st": 0.606,
   "range_st": 8.583,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 102.724,
   "e": 110.764,
   "text": "These functional circuits emerge entirely without any dynamic topological rewiring during inference.",
   "dur": 8.04,
   "voiced": 492,
   "sim": 0.868,
   "f0": 126.623,
   "st": -0.187,
   "range_st": 7.962,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 111.363,
   "e": 114.531,
   "text": "The weights remain completely fixed,",
   "dur": 3.168,
   "voiced": 140,
   "sim": 0.787,
   "f0": 124.814,
   "st": -0.436,
   "range_st": 6.048,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 114.733,
   "e": 122.482,
   "text": "yet the activation flow exhibits extraordinary dynamic routing and multi-step algorithmic execution.",
   "dur": 7.749,
   "voiced": 464,
   "sim": 0.847,
   "f0": 130.56,
   "st": 0.343,
   "range_st": 8.213,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 123.462,
   "e": 132.481,
   "text": "In seminal work by Olsson and colleagues, attention heads coordinate across layers to form induction circuits,",
   "dur": 9.019,
   "voiced": 476,
   "sim": 0.873,
   "f0": 134.716,
   "st": 0.885,
   "range_st": 9.992,
   "asr": 0.938,
   "attempts": 5,
   "level": 2
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 133.007,
   "e": 137.453,
   "text": "which appear to be a mechanistic source of in-context learning.",
   "dur": 4.446,
   "voiced": 253,
   "sim": 0.818,
   "f0": 124.961,
   "st": -0.416,
   "range_st": 8.571,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 138.544,
   "e": 146.223,
   "text": "When an induction head operates, it copies previous tokens based on bilinear query-key matching,",
   "dur": 7.678,
   "voiced": 433,
   "sim": 0.891,
   "f0": 135.379,
   "st": 0.97,
   "range_st": 9.628,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 146.472,
   "e": 150.725,
   "text": "effectively retrieving arbitrary associative context.",
   "dur": 4.253,
   "voiced": 234,
   "sim": 0.809,
   "f0": 136.328,
   "st": 1.091,
   "range_st": 8.109,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 151.131,
   "e": 160.836,
   "text": "Biologically-inspired local plasticity rules cannot perform this token-specific lookup without catastrophic interference.",
   "dur": 9.706,
   "voiced": 504,
   "sim": 0.859,
   "f0": 121.08,
   "st": -0.962,
   "range_st": 6.912,
   "asr": 0.897,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 161.853,
   "e": 175.375,
   "text": "How could a rigid, non-biological monolith spontaneously evolve the very modular reasoning that biologically-inspired self-organizing networks failed to produce?",
   "dur": 13.522,
   "voiced": 801,
   "sim": 0.855,
   "f0": 121.599,
   "st": -0.888,
   "range_st": 6.301,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 175.595,
   "e": 183.042,
   "text": "This paradox cannot be explained away by dataset size or engineering patience alone.",
   "dur": 7.447,
   "voiced": 442,
   "sim": 0.869,
   "f0": 131.006,
   "st": 0.402,
   "range_st": 7.111,
   "asr": 0.889,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 184.148,
